# I. Corporate profile

# Main battalion business

MarketAxes is the leading global fixed-income electronic trading platform operator, established in 2000 and headquartered in New York. Through its proprietary technology platform, the company provides corporate bonds, emerging market bonds, European bonds, United States bonds and other fixed-income securities with electronic trading services for institutional investors and brokers.

The company core product Open Trading is a recognized worldwide market-to-all credit-debt-trading solution that allows buyers and sellers to interface directly, breaking down traditional brokering patterns. By 2025, about 2,100 agencies and brokers had customers using the platform in some 90 countries.

## Income structure (2025)

- **Treat commission income**: about 86.8 per cent of total income is a core source of revenue. This includes transaction fees for such items as United States investment-level corporate debt, high-yield debt, emerging market debt, European bonds, United States Treasury debt, etc.
- ** Income from services** (information services, post-trading services, technical services): about 13.2 per cent of the total revenue from services in 2024 amounted to a record $105.4 million, an increase of 18 per cent over the same period, including the revenue from technical services from the acquisition of Pragma

Market position

- The market share of electronic transactions of United States investment-level companies in debt is estimated at approximately 85 per cent (estimated)
- Market share of the United States high-yield portfolio of debt, approximately 22.6 per cent (Q3 2025)
- One of the pioneers and leaders in the field of electronic trading of credit debt worldwide
Open Trading processed about $1.2 trillion in credit debt transactions in 2025.

