# V. Risk factors

#1. Increased competition — the continuing threat of Tradeweb
Tradeweb Markets has already placed substantial competitive pressure on MarketAxes in the area of investment-level credit debts, and has been a leading platform for e-investment-level credit debts for more than a quarter of a century in 2025. If MarketAxes continues to lose market shares, its network effects could be caught in a negative cycle.

##2. Double risk of volume and pricing
Companies’ income is highly dependent on transactional commissions (about 87%). If bond markets are less active (e.g., interest rate fluctuations and narrow credit spreads), revenue will be directly impaired.

#3 Changes in the structure of fixed-income markets
While there is still room for upgrading the e-commerce rate of bond markets, the role of MarketAxes as an intermediary may be challenged if large banks and marketers build their own e-trade platforms or regulatory changes affect market structures.

##4. Valuation still has downside space
Although the current valuation is below historical averages, it may not be sufficiently inexpensive if the sustained loss of market share leads to a permanent decline in growth to less than 5 per cent.

5. Macroeconomic risk
The recession may lead to a reduction in credit debt issuance and transaction activity, with direct effects on corporate income.

